%% Negative: nested-union coverage gap at a list head — vGLP's reported repro.
%%
%% Source: vGLP's input-coverage bug report of 2026-07-09, retired to
%% vGLP/OLD/ once the defect was closed; the repro is kept here, at vGLP's
%% request of 2026-07-31, so the regression is argued from the suite rather than
%% from a retired report.
%%
%% MyList's element type Color declares `red` and `blue`, and no clause handles
%% blue, so the input path MyList -> [|] -> blue is accepted by no clause
%% (Well-Typed GLP Program cond. 2). Catching it needs the checker to descend
%% into the Color union nested under the list constructor and re-resolve the
%% automaton owning each of its states, which is what carries coverage across a
%% type reference into a nested union. The checker must reject this program.
%%
%% Same defect as counter_missing_updown.glp beside it; this is the shape that
%% escaped.
Color ::= red ; blue.
MyList ::= [] ; [Color | MyList].
procedure g(MyList?, MyList).
g([red|Rest], [red|Rest1?]) :- g(Rest?, Rest1).
g([], []).
